hings that lie outside of our  control and we'll talk quite a bit about  the consequences which tend to be kind  of bad for us in confusing these two  categories we'll also go a little bit  more into detail about what it is that  that Epictetus does think it is in our  control including this term prior ASIS  or faculty choice that he sees at the  core of the person our emotions our  beliefs our desires our versions and  then we'll talk about the things that he  says lie outside of our control what the  Stoics call externals or indifference  and that will lead quite naturally into  some challenges or some objections to  this this whole idea because the Stoics  say things that are pretty paradoxical  like our bodies are not in our control  our finances are not in our control and  so we'll have to do a little bit of talk  at that well to what degree are they  this will lead naturally into a new  proposal that was put forth by William  Irvine who wrote a great book about  stoicism several years back saying that  maybe we should think about it not in  terms of by dichotomy of control but a  trichotomy of control this sort of 2/3  and we'll look at his proposal and  whether it works well or not and then  we'll talk about what epictetus himself  specifically has to say about you know  the things and the dimensions that are  in our control there are some external  things which themselves are not in our  controller where outcomes aren't in our  control but our use or how we deal with  them is epic team says that is in our  control and that happens to be very  important and we'll finish by talking  about how we might expand or in some  ways consolidate what is in our control  so we can have a life that's more free  more happy a life of flourishing as the  Stoics conceived of it at this point  you're probably asking yourself  three important questions when where and  how when are these online events where  do they actually meet and how do I sign  up for them so let me start with the  where we use freeconferencecall.com  which is a video conferencing platform  and we have our own meeting space which  you'll jump into if you participate in  either of these kinds of events now the  when very important and and I do want to  preface this by saying not only do you  want to mark your calendar you also want  to check your time zone because all of  the times that we're giving are for  central time that is Chicago time that's  the time zone that I'm in so May 16th  which is a Tuesday at 12:00 p.m.  running from 12 p.m. to 12:45 p.m. it is  the free webinar anybody can participate  in that we can have as many participants  as we can we can you know find but you  know you do want to have questions ready  ahead of time and then the online  intensive seminars we actually have two  of these I should mention as well these  are not different from each other  they're just different times we have  those on Saturday May 20th one starts at  10 a.m. and runs to 12 p.m. the other  one starts at 4:00 p.m. and runs to 6  p.m. again Central Time now why do we  have two of these well we only have 12  seats available for each of them because  we want this to be a much more intensive  and intimate experience getting to  interact and and talk about these issues  we try to keep them as budget friendly  as possible so enrollment in those  online seminars is $49 the webinar is  completely free of course and you might  want to check out the webinar just to  get a taste to see if you might be  interested in the seminars I'm very  excited to teach and talk about this  this great material with you Epictetus  is one of my favorite philosophers as a  matter of fact I'll even put a link  below to a interview that I did  I said that Epictetus is discourses is  one of the three books that most changed  my life  a little bit of a digression there in  any case check out the the descriptions  check out the links sign up for these  events seats are going to go quick I  think for the online seminars because  there is such a massive interest in  stoic philosophy at this time and I look  forward to seeing you there  [Music]

